WEBVTT

00:39.559 --> 00:41.892
And now,
The History Channel presents

00:41.928 --> 00:45.663
The True Story of Henry Ford.

00:45.698 --> 00:47.999
This is my Jew Flattening Machine.

00:48.034 --> 00:49.600
It'll flatten any Jew.

00:49.636 --> 00:50.901
Simply climb behind the wheel,

00:50.937 --> 00:52.703
drive it towards a Jew, and flatten him.

00:52.739 --> 00:54.405
Could you also use it just to drive

00:54.440 --> 00:56.073
from place to place and stuff?

00:56.109 --> 00:57.508
It-It's a Jew Flattening Machine.

00:57.543 --> 00:58.776
It's not what it's designed for.

00:58.811 --> 01:00.244
But you could use it that way?

01:00.280 --> 01:02.013
Yeah, yeah, you cou...
Yeah, yeah, you-you could

01:02.048 --> 01:05.116
also use the Mona Lisa
as a placemat. God.

01:05.151 --> 01:06.651
- Hey, guys.
- Oh, hey, Quagmire.

01:06.686 --> 01:08.452
How was marching band practice?

01:08.488 --> 01:10.788
Peter, you know
this is a pilot's uniform.

01:10.823 --> 01:13.057
It represents years
of specialized training.

01:13.092 --> 01:14.492
Yeah, well, you know
what else takes years

01:14.527 --> 01:16.761
of specialized training?
Crossing your eyes.

01:18.965 --> 01:20.798
Aah! Aah! Aah! Too far! Too far!

01:20.833 --> 01:22.800
Hold still.

01:25.738 --> 01:27.972
Thank you, Korean sweatshop animator.

01:28.007 --> 01:30.141
You've earned your nickel this week.

01:30.176 --> 01:31.609
Where're you coming from, Quagmire?

01:31.644 --> 01:34.078
I had to fly to Aruba,
so I brought my mom along

01:34.113 --> 01:35.880
with my "friends and family" discount.

01:35.915 --> 01:36.881
Did you...

01:36.916 --> 01:39.450
Yes, Joe, I got you a magnet.

01:39.485 --> 01:41.619
Where do you even
put all those magnets, Joe?

01:41.654 --> 01:43.721
Well, you know I have
that fridge in the garage

01:43.756 --> 01:45.756
with bags of blood in my blood type?

01:47.727 --> 01:49.293
What's "friends and family"?

01:49.329 --> 01:51.329
Oh, airline employees
can get discounted tickets

01:51.364 --> 01:53.064
for family and close friends.

01:53.099 --> 01:55.499
What? How-how come
you've never done that for us?

01:55.535 --> 01:57.001
If I'm being honest, I've also got

01:57.036 --> 01:58.636
a few Celeste pizzas in that fridge.

01:58.671 --> 02:00.771
I don't know, I-I guess
I just figured you guys

02:00.807 --> 02:02.673
always have to work,
or you're with your kids.

02:02.709 --> 02:04.308
But sure, yeah,
I could take you somewhere.

02:04.344 --> 02:06.777
I'm going to San Francisco next
week. You guys want to come?

02:06.813 --> 02:08.312
San Francisco?

02:08.348 --> 02:10.548
That city from And the Band
Played On and Milk?

02:10.583 --> 02:11.749
I'm in!

02:11.784 --> 02:13.250
Yeah, thanks, Quagmire.

02:13.286 --> 02:14.885
Oh, wow, this'll be great.

02:14.921 --> 02:16.921
Hey, can you make us X-Men?

02:20.393 --> 02:22.560
What a surprise.

02:26.632 --> 02:28.766
Well, I'm off to San Francisco
with the guys.

02:28.801 --> 02:31.502
Okay, I'm off to Hilton Head
with the girls.

02:31.537 --> 02:32.703
- You what?
- Peter,

02:32.739 --> 02:34.939
I told you about this a month ago.

02:34.974 --> 02:36.440
I'm going with Bonnie and Donna

02:36.476 --> 02:38.209
to Donna's sister's time share.

02:38.244 --> 02:40.711
Well, we can't both
go on a trip at the same time.

02:40.747 --> 02:43.981
I'm sorry, Peter, but I already
have a taxi waiting.

02:44.016 --> 02:47.151
All right, I'll go
tell the guys I'm not going.

02:47.186 --> 02:49.687
Why is he taking his suitcase
to tell the guys?

02:49.722 --> 02:51.655
You guys, come on, we got to
go now. Let's go, move it.

02:51.691 --> 02:53.023
I'm in the shower.
It doesn't matter,

02:53.059 --> 02:55.826
we're stealing Lois' cab.

02:55.862 --> 02:57.228
Son of a...

02:57.263 --> 03:01.065
Oh, and the idiot took my suitcase.

03:01.100 --> 03:04.969
Aw, he was taking me with him.

03:11.711 --> 03:14.245
Ah, San Francisco.

03:14.280 --> 03:16.480
Aah! San Francisco!

03:16.516 --> 03:17.948
So what are we gonna do first?

03:17.984 --> 03:19.483
I want to see the Golden Gate Bridge.

03:19.519 --> 03:21.118
I want to see Lombard Street.

03:21.154 --> 03:22.553
I want to see Ghirardelli Square.

03:22.588 --> 03:23.854
Guys, guys.

03:23.890 --> 03:27.224
Let's get lesbian
haircuts and see 'em all.

03:47.079 --> 03:48.746
All right, the gay jokes
are out of the way,

03:48.781 --> 03:50.614
now let's get down to business.

03:54.654 --> 03:58.022
Okay, guys, this is the
original Levi Jeans factory,

03:58.057 --> 04:01.559
created by Levi Strauss in the year 1853

04:01.594 --> 04:04.361
so that gold miners could wear a
comfortable yet durable fabric.

04:04.397 --> 04:05.763
This is boring.

04:05.798 --> 04:07.498
Well, then you plan the vacation!

04:07.533 --> 04:08.732
Aah!

04:08.768 --> 04:10.668
Peter, Peter, calm down, it-it's okay,

04:10.703 --> 04:12.102
we'll-we'll do whatever you want.

04:12.138 --> 04:13.704
All right, if you promise.

04:13.739 --> 04:16.006
I was thinkin' we could
tuck our shirts into our pants,

04:16.042 --> 04:18.709
put on huge helmets, and ride Segways.

04:18.744 --> 04:22.012
We're not from here!
We're not from here!

04:24.826 --> 04:25.983
You guys, look.

04:26.018 --> 04:28.853
It's Golden State Warriors
star Steph Curry.

04:29.989 --> 04:31.889
Oh, my God, Steph, I'm such a big fan.

04:31.924 --> 04:33.424
Thanks. It's nice to meet you.

04:33.459 --> 04:35.759
Hey, I know we just met,
but can I sit on your lap

04:35.795 --> 04:37.828
during your next
post-game press conference?

04:37.864 --> 04:39.830
Sure, I don't see why not.

04:39.866 --> 04:41.699
This is exciting for the whole Bay Area,

04:41.734 --> 04:44.034
to be just four games away
from the championship...

04:44.070 --> 04:45.336
Dad, I dooked.

04:45.371 --> 04:47.304
That other team's not just
gonna go away, though.

04:47.340 --> 04:49.707
We've got to stay focused, keep
doing what we've been doing.

04:49.742 --> 04:52.209
Fat lady. Dad, Dad, a fat lady.

04:52.245 --> 04:53.544
Yeah, I-I see her, Peter.

04:53.579 --> 04:54.778
Make her go.

04:54.814 --> 04:56.280
That's not how we talk to people.

04:56.315 --> 04:57.481
Make her go.

04:57.517 --> 04:58.682
I'll leave.

04:58.718 --> 05:01.418
Yay! I'm learning bad lessons.

05:06.659 --> 05:09.260
Wow. So that was San Francisco.

05:09.295 --> 05:11.862
I didn't realize
how hilly it was gonna be.

05:11.898 --> 05:13.731
Thanks again for taking us, Quagmire.

05:13.766 --> 05:14.965
Hey, no problem.

05:15.001 --> 05:16.200
Hey, you know, we're here early.

05:16.235 --> 05:18.068
You guys want a little
tour of the plane?

05:18.104 --> 05:19.270
Yeah, that'd be great.

05:19.305 --> 05:21.005
Normally I'd just go to Hudson News

05:21.040 --> 05:23.607
and pretend to be
the most important guy there.

05:23.643 --> 05:24.708
Can I help you?

05:24.744 --> 05:26.777
Yes, I will have eight Dasanis

05:26.812 --> 05:29.013
and a JD Power & Associates.

05:34.854 --> 05:36.620
Wow, this place is cool.

05:36.656 --> 05:38.689
Yeah. What do all these buttons do?

05:38.724 --> 05:40.157
Like, what's this red one?

05:40.192 --> 05:42.593
Oh, that's a voice filter,
so the passengers always think

05:42.628 --> 05:45.029
the pilot is a 60-year-old
Midwestern white man.

05:45.064 --> 05:47.231
What? That's impossible.

05:47.266 --> 05:49.667
Hi y'all, this is Cleveland.

05:49.702 --> 05:51.035
Good afternoon, folks,

05:51.070 --> 05:53.404
this is Captain Dale Clark
up here in the flight deck.

05:53.439 --> 05:55.472
We're way up in the air.

05:55.508 --> 05:58.809
We've reached our cruising
altitude of 37,000 feet.

05:58.844 --> 06:01.645
Y'all get ready to watch
Big Momma's House.

06:01.681 --> 06:03.113
Our in-flight entertainment today

06:03.149 --> 06:05.015
will be Under the Tuscan Sun.

06:05.051 --> 06:06.216
Ooh, I like that.

06:06.252 --> 06:07.551
I hear it's good.

06:07.587 --> 06:09.587
Hey, what's this button? "Autopilot"?

06:09.622 --> 06:12.323
Oh, that allows the plane to fly
itself when I need a break.

06:12.358 --> 06:13.591
W-What do you mean, "a break"?

06:13.659 --> 06:15.025
You don't have to fly the plane?

06:15.061 --> 06:17.595
Of course I do. I just take
a short break sometimes.

06:17.630 --> 06:19.930
Short break? It looks like you had time

06:19.966 --> 06:22.833
to put together
the 10,000-piece Lego Hogwarts.

06:22.868 --> 06:25.736
You don't have to touch it, Joe,
you can just say you noticed it.

06:25.771 --> 06:27.705
And what's this booth over here?

06:27.740 --> 06:29.373
Oh, that's my back-in-time box.

06:29.408 --> 06:31.408
I go inside, magically go back in time,

06:31.444 --> 06:34.044
and then come out and react
to the fact that we're flying.

06:36.349 --> 06:38.382
By God, we're levitating.

06:38.417 --> 06:40.284
That's just a box full of costumes.

06:40.319 --> 06:41.852
It's my back-in-time box!

06:41.887 --> 06:43.954
What the hell, Quagmire?
So-so, basically,

06:43.990 --> 06:45.389
your job is just goofin' off.

06:45.424 --> 06:46.423
That's not true.

06:46.459 --> 06:47.958
I broke Gandalf in half.

06:47.994 --> 06:48.959
It's Dumbledore!

06:48.995 --> 06:50.594
Screw you guys. You know, being a pilot

06:50.630 --> 06:52.663
is hard work. Look, I tried to be nice

06:52.698 --> 06:54.365
and take you fellas on a free trip,

06:54.400 --> 06:56.634
and all you can do
is crap all over my job.

06:56.669 --> 06:58.769
I was a Navy pilot, you jerks.

06:58.804 --> 07:00.437
Get the hell out of my cockpit.

07:03.109 --> 07:05.876
Joke's on him. I farted
just before he kicked us out.

07:05.911 --> 07:08.212
Ugh. Oh, God!

07:13.285 --> 07:15.677
All right, let's see what's
in the in-flight magazine.

07:16.111 --> 07:17.788
Muscular old guy.

07:17.823 --> 07:20.124
Already filled-in crossword puzzle.

07:20.159 --> 07:23.293
Ooh, this is food
for different routes I'm not on.

07:24.830 --> 07:26.563
All right, time to use the potty.

07:26.599 --> 07:28.966
Don't say "potty." You're an adult.

07:35.141 --> 07:37.474
Okay, nobody move!

07:37.510 --> 07:40.444
Oh, my God, those guys
in first class have guns.

07:40.479 --> 07:42.312
Cleveland, just be happy
with what you have.

07:42.348 --> 07:43.514
Don't envy people.

07:43.549 --> 07:45.349
No, Peter, we're being hijacked.

07:45.384 --> 07:46.884
Close the cockpit door!

07:51.023 --> 07:52.990
This plane now belongs to us.

07:53.025 --> 07:54.591
You move, you're dead.

07:54.627 --> 07:56.660
So nobody try to get smart.

07:56.696 --> 07:59.363
Mm, page 100. Mm.

08:03.480 --> 08:05.880
Control tower, this is flight 364.

08:05.916 --> 08:07.615
We have a hijacking in progress.

08:07.651 --> 08:09.317
Our flight has been...

08:09.352 --> 08:11.419
Oh, damn it,
they jammed the transmission.

08:11.454 --> 08:13.922
I'm gonna have to go to
the backup communication system.

08:18.495 --> 08:19.994
Hello? Can you hear me?

08:20.030 --> 08:21.529
This is Flight 364.

08:21.565 --> 08:22.864
We're being hijacked.

08:22.899 --> 08:24.265
I can hear you... Oh!

08:29.339 --> 08:30.672
This is your last chance.

08:30.707 --> 08:33.241
Open the door, or your copilot gets it.

08:33.276 --> 08:35.276
No. I'm landing at the closest airfield,

08:35.312 --> 08:38.079
which is less than an hour away.
So just let him go,

08:38.114 --> 08:40.081
'cause you're not
getting control of this plane.

08:41.117 --> 08:43.551
Aah! Jimmy! Oh, my God!

08:43.587 --> 08:44.786
Why are you doing this?

08:44.821 --> 08:46.321
America needs to be punished

08:46.356 --> 08:49.357
for supporting the other side
of my country's civil war.

08:49.392 --> 08:50.658
Which country?

08:50.694 --> 08:51.993
Do you really want to know,

08:52.028 --> 08:53.494
or are you just asking because

08:53.530 --> 08:55.430
we're gonna be on a plane for a while

08:55.465 --> 08:57.765
and you think you
should make small talk?

08:57.801 --> 08:59.634
The second thing.

08:59.669 --> 09:00.969
Open the door, or I'll start

09:01.004 --> 09:03.638
executing passengers.

09:03.673 --> 09:06.841
Man, coming on this trip
was a terrible idea.

09:06.876 --> 09:08.943
I know, now I wish I'd just stayed home

09:08.979 --> 09:11.412
and finished my remake of Inside Out.

09:11.448 --> 09:12.614
I'm Joy.

09:12.649 --> 09:13.982
I'm Sadness.

09:14.017 --> 09:15.049
I'm Anger.

09:15.085 --> 09:16.317
I'm Disgust.

09:16.353 --> 09:18.386
I'm Poo.

09:19.456 --> 09:22.257
Ooh, I need to use the bathroom.

09:22.292 --> 09:24.459
Yay! I win!

09:30.367 --> 09:32.300
We interrupt this program
with a special report.

09:32.335 --> 09:34.502
A flight from San Francisco to Quahog

09:34.537 --> 09:36.971
has lost contact
with air traffic control.

09:37.007 --> 09:39.774
Oh, my God, that's your father's flight.

09:39.809 --> 09:40.842
Government officials

09:40.877 --> 09:42.410
are monitoring the situation closely.

09:42.445 --> 09:44.846
I'll be here to update you
as this story progresses.

09:44.881 --> 09:47.382
Coming up on the midday news,
a couple in their 30s

09:47.417 --> 09:49.751
gets married without their dog
being in the wedding.

09:49.786 --> 09:52.086
You're not gonna believe their story.

09:55.191 --> 09:56.324
What's it gonna be?

09:56.359 --> 09:57.692
Are you going to open this door,

09:57.727 --> 09:59.294
or am I going to start killing people?

09:59.329 --> 10:00.628
I'm not opening it.

10:00.664 --> 10:02.830
Excuse me, I'd just like to ask
the mom behind me

10:02.866 --> 10:05.366
who told me to stop watching
Game of Thrones on my laptop

10:05.402 --> 10:09.370
if I'm still "the worst person
on this plane."

10:09.406 --> 10:11.105
You, fat guy. Get up here!

10:11.141 --> 10:12.473
Aah!

10:14.010 --> 10:15.343
Last chance. Open the door,

10:15.378 --> 10:16.978
or this idiot gets it.

10:17.013 --> 10:18.646
Don't open it, Quagmire.
It's not worth it.

10:18.682 --> 10:19.847
Okay.

10:19.883 --> 10:21.316
Wait... wait, what?

10:21.351 --> 10:22.884
That-that was quick.

10:22.919 --> 10:25.486
I'm sorry, Peter, but I have
to think about the whole plane.

10:25.522 --> 10:27.789
There's over 150 passengers back there,

10:27.824 --> 10:29.824
several of whom are in
our Commander's Club,

10:29.859 --> 10:32.493
and to them I'd like to
issue a special welcome.

10:32.529 --> 10:34.162
Oh, man, we got to help Peter!

10:34.197 --> 10:36.764
Those crazy European guys
are gonna kill him!

10:36.800 --> 10:39.033
You know, I have a gun
in the bag I checked.

10:39.069 --> 10:40.568
If we can get to the galley,

10:40.603 --> 10:43.204
we can take the elevator
down to the cargo hold.

10:43.239 --> 10:44.872
Good idea, Joe.

10:44.908 --> 10:48.543
Oh, man, it feels like we're in
one of those hijacking movies.

10:48.578 --> 10:51.145
You're right, it does. There's
even an impatient businessman

10:51.181 --> 10:53.147
who really wants to
reach his destination

10:53.183 --> 10:55.516
so he can conduct more business.

10:55.552 --> 10:57.185
Can't you see how important I am?

10:57.220 --> 10:59.187
My shirt is blue, but
the collar is white.

10:59.222 --> 11:00.922
It's the same shirt!

11:00.957 --> 11:02.957
Quick, he's distracted.

11:11.497 --> 11:13.067
"Get off my plane."

11:13.103 --> 11:15.336
"Get off my plane."

11:15.372 --> 11:16.738
- What's that, now?
- Hmm?

11:16.773 --> 11:18.152
Nothing.

11:18.863 --> 11:20.942
"Always bet on black."

11:20.977 --> 11:22.543
"Always bet on black."

11:22.579 --> 11:24.545
- Did you say something?
- I don't think so.

11:26.182 --> 11:27.682
- "Double trouble!"
- "Double trouble!"

11:27.717 --> 11:29.550
That's it. We found it.

11:30.261 --> 11:31.285
What the hell?!

11:31.321 --> 11:34.222
Hey! Two of the passengers are missing!

11:34.257 --> 11:35.823
Okay, you guys watch the main cabin.

11:35.859 --> 11:36.991
I'll go find them.

11:37.026 --> 11:39.427
I'll take this fat guy
as a human shield.

11:39.462 --> 11:41.562
Oh, nice. Last guy picked for dodgeball,

11:41.598 --> 11:43.731
first guy for human shield.

11:47.270 --> 11:49.103
Everybody be quiet!

11:49.139 --> 11:50.905
There's another update!

11:50.940 --> 11:52.306
Good afternoon. I'm Tom Tucker.

11:52.342 --> 11:54.509
The search for
a missing airliner continues,

11:54.544 --> 11:57.645
as speculation grows that
the plane has been hijacked.

11:57.680 --> 11:59.647
Oh, this is all so awful!

11:59.682 --> 12:03.117
What will our lives be like
if our husbands don't make it?

12:28.211 --> 12:31.646
Oh, my God! Now I want Dad to die!

12:35.389 --> 12:37.351
Hey, Joe, look at me.

12:37.387 --> 12:39.287
Do I look like Mickey the Mouse?

12:39.322 --> 12:40.888
Get out of people's stuff!

12:40.924 --> 12:42.790
Ah, here's my bag.

12:45.995 --> 12:48.763
Hey! What are you two doing down here?

12:51.234 --> 12:53.868
Oh, someone's shipping live lobsters.

12:53.903 --> 12:55.403
Yum.

12:55.438 --> 12:56.404
Prepare to die.

12:56.439 --> 12:57.538
You first!

12:57.574 --> 12:59.774
That's what you think.

13:02.479 --> 13:04.412
Peter! Grab on to something!

13:04.447 --> 13:06.881
Uh-oh. I grabbed my own belt.

13:27.303 --> 13:30.204
Attention, passengers,
I know we're being hijacked,

13:30.240 --> 13:32.039
but I would be remiss
if I didn't point out

13:32.075 --> 13:34.976
that we're presently passing
over Yosemite National Park.

13:35.011 --> 13:38.246
Wow! That is truly awe-inspiring!

13:38.281 --> 13:39.714
It certainly is.

13:39.749 --> 13:41.716
And you know what you don't see
from up here?

13:41.751 --> 13:43.451
Borders.

13:49.659 --> 13:52.560
Die in hell, Eurotrash!

13:52.595 --> 13:54.028
Hang on, Peter!

13:56.099 --> 13:58.733
Holy crap, that was close.

13:58.768 --> 14:01.068
Joe, how'd you know that lever
would open the landing gear?

14:01.104 --> 14:02.803
Wheels are my expertise, Peter.

14:02.839 --> 14:06.107
I notice every wheel in
a room as soon as I enter.

14:09.345 --> 14:12.446
Special delivery from the U.S. of A.!

14:13.983 --> 14:14.982
Aw, rats.

14:15.018 --> 14:16.918
My bullets are in my shaving kit.

14:24.297 --> 14:26.174
Get off my pl... Double trouble!

14:26.210 --> 14:28.629
Sorry. Come on, man!

14:30.366 --> 14:31.666
Oh, my God, you guys did it!

14:31.701 --> 14:32.833
We're saved!

14:32.869 --> 14:34.435
Yep, we wrapped this up quicker

14:34.470 --> 14:36.571
than the treaty signing at Appomattox.

14:36.606 --> 14:39.106
So, if I sign this, the war is over,

14:39.142 --> 14:42.643
we surrender, and we still
get to be dicks forever?

14:42.679 --> 14:45.307
Okay, you win.

14:45.848 --> 14:47.315
You can all relax now, everybody!

14:47.350 --> 14:48.783
We're ten minutes away from landing

14:48.818 --> 14:50.284
at an airfield in Nevada.

14:50.320 --> 14:53.154
Looks like you'll make
that business meeting after all.

14:53.189 --> 14:56.557
Great! Thanks for keeping us
in the sky, boys.

14:56.593 --> 14:58.559
Now reach for it.

14:58.595 --> 15:00.628
You're one of the hijackers, too?!

15:00.663 --> 15:04.298
Yes. I was in reserve in
case the plan went awry.

15:04.334 --> 15:06.567
And now I can finally get
into the cockpit

15:06.603 --> 15:08.235
and execute our plan:

15:08.271 --> 15:10.504
crashing this plane
into the ultimate symbol

15:10.540 --> 15:12.173
of American materialism,

15:12.208 --> 15:14.141
Las Vegas.

15:14.177 --> 15:16.277
You know, I've lost a ton in Vegas,

15:16.312 --> 15:18.679
but I never thought
I'd lose my life there.

15:18.715 --> 15:21.082
- Did you just think of that?
- Yeah, just now.

15:21.117 --> 15:23.217
You know, you are seriously funny, man.

15:23.252 --> 15:25.286
I know I crap on you
a lot, but sometimes,

15:25.321 --> 15:28.122
when I'm driving, I think
about stuff you say and I laugh.

15:28.157 --> 15:30.391
- Thank you, Peter.
- No, thank you.

15:35.352 --> 15:38.653
Very good. We are less than
20 minutes from Las Vegas.

15:38.688 --> 15:42.857
Get ready to say good-bye
to your precious Rita Rudner.

15:42.893 --> 15:45.593
Is-is your plan
just to kill Rita Rudner?

15:45.629 --> 15:48.930
No. We're going to crash into
the biggest hotel on the Strip!

15:48.965 --> 15:52.800
Killing Rita Rudner will just be
the custard on the dumpling.

15:52.836 --> 15:54.269
You know, we never quite nailed down

15:54.304 --> 15:56.504
what region you guys are from.

16:00.810 --> 16:02.443
Good afternoon.
I'm Tom Tucker with the latest

16:02.479 --> 16:03.845
on the hijacking crisis.

16:03.880 --> 16:05.780
As you can see, I've taken off my blazer

16:05.815 --> 16:07.649
to show the severity of the situation.

16:07.684 --> 16:10.318
We understand the plane
has been found by satellite.

16:10.353 --> 16:12.253
It's apparently veered off
its flight plan

16:12.289 --> 16:13.988
and is headed for Las Vegas.

16:14.024 --> 16:15.590
The government, fearing the worst,

16:15.625 --> 16:17.392
is considering shooting it down.

16:17.427 --> 16:19.994
Now here's an over-the-top news graphic.

16:22.232 --> 16:24.799
Nightmare over Vegas.

16:26.503 --> 16:30.638
Hijack Jackpot.

16:35.445 --> 16:37.712
Oh, look, there's one guy who
slept through this whole thing.

16:37.747 --> 16:39.080
Hey, buddy, wake up.

16:39.115 --> 16:40.548
We're all about to die.

16:40.583 --> 16:42.283
What? What are you talking about?

16:42.319 --> 16:43.751
Yeah, I thought I should wake you up.

16:43.787 --> 16:45.219
Nobody wants to die in their sleep.

16:45.255 --> 16:47.722
Oh, my God! No! I have a family!

16:47.757 --> 16:50.158
There you go.

16:50.193 --> 16:52.560
Only a few more minutes
until your country pays

16:52.595 --> 16:54.696
for its imperialistic sins.

16:54.731 --> 16:56.397
Us? What about you?!

16:56.433 --> 16:58.333
Like-like, how come
you Eastern European guys

16:58.368 --> 17:00.001
can't be quieter in pornos?

17:00.036 --> 17:03.037
I mean, nobody's ever been like,
"Yeah, yeah, more guy noises."

17:03.073 --> 17:04.839
They ask us to do that
to cover up the sound

17:04.874 --> 17:06.374
of children playing nearby.

17:06.409 --> 17:09.010
Now shut up and get ready to die.

17:17.320 --> 17:20.021
So, uh, you ever been to Vegas before?

17:20.056 --> 17:21.189
No.

17:21.224 --> 17:22.857
Well, I think you're gonna...

17:22.892 --> 17:24.359
flip for it!

17:32.769 --> 17:35.403
Attention, passengers, the plane...

17:37.774 --> 17:40.942
Oh, come on! Doesn't anybody
pay attention to the sign?!

17:45.015 --> 17:46.714
That was some quick thinking, Glenn.

17:46.750 --> 17:49.984
And look! Even that plane with
all the missiles is impressed.

17:52.022 --> 17:54.655
Missiles? That's a military fighter jet!

17:54.691 --> 17:56.324
He's here to shoot us down!

17:56.359 --> 17:58.426
- Or "she."
- What?!

17:58.461 --> 18:00.595
They must think the hijackers
still control the plane!

18:00.630 --> 18:01.996
And our communications are jammed,

18:02.032 --> 18:04.065
so we can't even tell them
everything's okay!

18:04.100 --> 18:05.900
Don't worry, I'll signal to 'em.

18:05.935 --> 18:08.736
Hey! We knocked out all the bad guys!

18:08.772 --> 18:10.405
See? We don't need your help!

18:10.440 --> 18:12.740
We kicked their asses
and we have their guns!

18:12.776 --> 18:14.542
I've got a visual on the terrorists.

18:14.577 --> 18:17.345
They've got a hostage in a blue
shirt with a white collar.

18:17.380 --> 18:19.013
He must be an important businessman.

18:19.049 --> 18:21.349
Copy that. Prepare to engage.

18:23.987 --> 18:25.486
Oh, good, he's movin' away.

18:25.522 --> 18:27.488
No, he isn't. He's g getting
in position to fire!

18:27.524 --> 18:29.290
He thinks we're gonna crash
into the Strip!

18:29.325 --> 18:30.792
Everybody in your seats!

18:52.415 --> 18:54.849
Frank Caliendo does a 5:00 show?

18:54.884 --> 18:56.818
Quagmire, land this plane!

19:04.194 --> 19:05.359
We've been hit!

19:07.097 --> 19:08.329
Oh, God, this is it!

19:08.364 --> 19:09.464
We're gonna die!

19:09.499 --> 19:10.598
Like hell we are!

19:10.633 --> 19:12.166
We're gonna make it.

19:26.249 --> 19:27.548
We're going too fast!

19:27.584 --> 19:29.350
We're gonna crash into that lake!

19:29.419 --> 19:32.220
Oh, no, we're not!

19:42.665 --> 19:45.299
Oh, yeah,
right there. That's good.

19:45.335 --> 19:48.836
And now to discharge
the plane's fire retardant.

19:48.872 --> 19:50.838
Giggity.

20:01.284 --> 20:03.985
Wow, Quagmire, thanks for
saving all of our lives.

20:04.343 --> 20:06.320
We're sorry for saying
your job was easy.

20:06.356 --> 20:08.523
Yeah, you're the best
damn pilot in the world.

20:08.558 --> 20:11.526
He's right. What you did
up there was amazing.

20:11.561 --> 20:13.327
Thanks, guys, that means a lot.

20:13.363 --> 20:15.062
Boy, that was quite a trip, wasn't it?

20:15.098 --> 20:18.266
Sure was. And we learned
a lot about blue jeans,

20:18.301 --> 20:20.268
- didn't we, guys?
- Yes, yes, we did, yeah.

20:20.303 --> 20:23.271
- That's right, Peter.
- Thank you for planning a wonderful day.

20:28.478 --> 20:29.980
- Cleveland!
- Joe!

20:30.016 --> 20:30.878
Peter!

20:36.961 --> 20:38.219
Dad, I was really worried,

20:38.254 --> 20:40.221
so I pulled a record
of your credit card purchases

20:40.256 --> 20:42.290
in San Francisco, and I saw some things

20:42.325 --> 20:44.225
I think you'd prefer to keep private.

20:44.260 --> 20:45.560
We'll talk later, Chris.

20:45.595 --> 20:47.161
I think we will.

20:47.197 --> 20:49.330
I do believe we will.

20:49.365 --> 20:50.731
Well, let's head home.

20:50.767 --> 20:53.467
I know I, for one, am ready
to put all this behind us.

20:53.503 --> 20:54.969
Sounds good.

20:55.004 --> 20:58.066
Oh, yeah, in case we didn't say,
this was Spirit Airlines.

20:58.067 --> 21:59.067
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru